{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/17/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/17`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/17/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：每个彩色区域按照其内部孔洞的数量，在区域周围绘制对应层数的同色轮廓环。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为主色（如 black）。\n  - 网格中有若干个不同颜色的实心或带孔洞的封闭区域（4-连通），彼此不接触且不重叠。\n  - 每个区域内部可能包含 0、1、2 或 3 个由背景色构成的孔洞（完全被该区域像素包围的背景连通区）。\n  - 区域之间有足够的背景空间容纳扩展的轮廓环。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保留所有原始区域不变（包括其孔洞）。\n  - 对每个区域，数出其内部孔洞的数量 N。\n  - 在该区域的外部，绘制 N 层同色的轮廓环。第一层轮廓环由所有与该区域 4-相邻的背景像素构成，第二层轮廓环由所有与第一层 4-相邻的背景像素构成，以此类推。\n  - 若轮廓环的扩展遇到网格边界或其他区域的像素则在该方向停止（但其他方向继续）。\n  - 没有孔洞（N=0）的区域不产生任何轮廓环。\n\n- `Key insight`：表面上看是简单的\"给区域加边框\"，但边框的层数不是固定的，而是由区域内部的孔洞数量控制——解题者必须发现\"内部孔洞数 = 外部轮廓层数\"这一非显然的映射关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/71e489b6, eval/8b7bacbf, eval/dbff022c, eval/e3721c99, eval/581f7754, train/aa62e3f4, eval/16b78196, eval/a25697e4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"71e489b6\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3789\nmechanism=0.4929\nlexical=0.0189\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, operation:count, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/71e489b6.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/71e489b6.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nHighlight black defects in blue foreground by surrounding them with orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- Blue (1) foreground on black (0) bg; small black holes or protrusions within blue regions; occasional thin blue spurs into black areas.\n\nRule:\n- Thin blue pixels mostly surrounded by black are absorbed into the background.\n- Small black components (≤3 cells) and leaf pixels of larger black components are \"defects.\"\n- Each defect gets an orange (7) 8-neighbor halo; the defect pixels themselves stay black.\n\nKey insight: Only structural anomalies—tiny isolated patches and dangling endpoints—are marked, not bulk black regions.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"small black sprite s in and on edge of blue foreground regions\",\n  \"transform\": \"surround s with orange\",\n  \"src2\": \"small blue sprite s2 in and on edge of black bg regions\",\n  \"transform2\": \"s2.color -> bg (disappear)\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3556\nmechanism=0.4009\nlexical=0.0148\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, operation:count, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3584\nmechanism=0.4347\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e3721c99\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3458\nmechanism=0.4286\nlexical=0.0146\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, object:sprite, operation:count, relation:adjacent, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/e3721c99.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e3721c99.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\n- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\n  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\n\nRule:\n- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\n- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\n- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\n\nKey insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Grey sprites in the grid are recolored based on matching their hole count to legend shapes, where each legend shape has a specific color and hole count.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"grey sprites scattered in the grid s\",\n  \"dst\": \"colored legend shapes in the top-left corner d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.hole_count == d.hole_count\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"s.color = d.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend shapes (colored sprites at grid edge) define color assignment: count holes in each legend shape; grey sprites with same hole count get recolored to that legend's color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"hole-counting\",\n    \"legend-matching\",\n    \"recoloring\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The difficulty lies in counting holes in each shape\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3155\nmechanism=0.3417\nlexical=0.0156\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3004\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
